{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.298bbe5ebb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-54","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kenji Haddad is a zoologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","To investigate the question, Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Because elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day, Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.ad00dd1c2f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-71","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Delacroix is a linguist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Delacroix gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Delacroix found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors, Delacroix concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","To investigate the question, Delacroix gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.","Delacroix concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","Delacroix found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.bc4ff5e4b6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-73","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Vance is an economist.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Vance tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Vance found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Vance concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Vance found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.","To investigate the question, Vance tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.","Vance concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Because output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly, Vance concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.73e47fb443","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-74","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Moreau is an economist.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Moreau tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Moreau found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Moreau concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly, Moreau concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Moreau found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.","Moreau concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","To investigate the question, Moreau tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.9e5941b3af","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-76","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Beatriz Rahman is an economist.</li><li>Rahman wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Rahman tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Rahman found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Rahman concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Rahman concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Because output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly, Rahman concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Rahman found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.","To investigate the question, Rahman tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.d080b180a4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-79","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Vance is a botanist.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Vance grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Vance found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Vance concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Vance grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Vance found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","Because plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates, Vance concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","Vance concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.57cef4265a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-80","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kenji Varga is a botanist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Varga grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Varga found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Varga concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","Because plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates, Varga concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","To investigate the question, Varga grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Varga concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.2c260df695","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-81","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Mensah is a botanist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Mensah grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Mensah found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Mensah concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","To investigate the question, Mensah grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Mensah found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","Because plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates, Mensah concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.916fa20a24","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-91","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Mei Halvorsen is a hydrologist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Halvorsen compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Halvorsen found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Halvorsen concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","To investigate the question, Halvorsen compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Halvorsen found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","Because river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands, Halvorsen concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.790f27be8a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-114","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Beatriz Mensah is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Mensah asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Mensah found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Mensah concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep, Mensah concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Mensah concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","To investigate the question, Mensah asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Mensah found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.d53e6e974a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-141","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Sato is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Sato scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Sato found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Sato concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sato found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","To investigate the question, Sato scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.","Because regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger, Sato concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Sato concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b5fc1a1ac8","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-145","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Takeda is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Takeda fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Takeda found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Takeda concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Takeda fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Takeda concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","Takeda found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.","Because kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser, Takeda concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.83a02c1b8c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-149","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Kowalski is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Kowalski fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Kowalski found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Kowalski found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.","Because kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser, Kowalski concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","Kowalski concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","To investigate the question, Kowalski fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.8e39d5cd52","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-162","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kenji Abara is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Abara played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Abara found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Abara concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Abara found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.","Because dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often, Abara concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","To investigate the question, Abara played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.","Abara concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b4694e41e0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-169","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Petrov is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Petrov wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Petrov added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Petrov found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Petrov concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks, Petrov concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","To investigate the question, Petrov added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Petrov found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","Petrov concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.2a38ea78a0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-175","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Omar Nakamura is a music researcher.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Nakamura tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Nakamura found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because children who took lessons improved more than those who did not, Nakamura concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","Nakamura concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","Nakamura found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.","To investigate the question, Nakamura tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."}
